{"name":"Leek Powder","hex":"#b7b17a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vegetable of variety Allium ampeloprasum, having edible leaves and an onion-like bulb but with a milder flavour than the onion.","Any of several species of Allium, broadly resembling the domesticated plant in appearance in the wild."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leek"},{"term":"powder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fine particles which are the result of reducing a dry substance by pounding, grinding, or triturating, or the result of decay; dust.\n\n Cocaine in powder form (as opposed to crack).","Cocaine in powder form (as opposed to crack)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reduce to fine particles; to pound, grind, or rub into a powder.","To sprinkle with powder, or as if with powder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leek","blocks":[{"text":"A leek is a biennial vegetable, a cultivar of Allium ampeloprasum, the broadleaf wild leek. The edible part of the plant is a bundle of leaf sheaths that is sometimes colloquially called a \"stem\" or \"stalk\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg/330px-Leek_on_white_background_-_0947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leek","wikidata":"Q1807269"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Iron_powder.JPG/330px-Iron_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder","wikidata":"Q2908004"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/500px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/1280px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG/500px-Leek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fresh leeks sautéing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeek-Saut%C3%A9.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/500px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/1280px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg/500px-%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leek soup","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%C4%8Cu%C5%A1pajz_od_poriluka_u_loncu.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Schuch_Still_life.jpg/500px-Schuch_Still_life.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Schuch_Still_lif